  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「キシュウスズメノヒエ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%AD%E3%82%B7%E3%83%A5%E3%82%A6%E3%82%B9%E3%82%BA%E3%83%A1%E3%83%8E%E3%83%92%E3%82%A8",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 106358228,
      "text": "キシュウスズメノヒエ Paspalum distichum L. は、イネ科の植物の一つで、よく這って伸びる多年草。水田などの雑草として注意が必要なものである。変種にチクゴスズメノヒエがある。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Paspalum distichum」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paspalum_distichum",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1306454174,
      "text": "Paspalum distichum is a species of grass. Common names include knotgrass, water finger-grass, couch paspalum, eternity grass, gingergrass, and Thompson grass. Its native range is obscure because it has long been present on most continents, and in most areas it is certainly an introduced species. Its native range probably includes parts of the tropical Americas."
    }
  },
